  era: "Section 11 \xB7 Post-Gupta Period \xB7 c. 550 \u2013 1000 CE"
  title: Chalukyas of Badami
  text: The Chalukyas of Badami, or Vatapi, in Karnataka, ruled the Deccan from the 6th to the 8th centuries. Pulakeshin the Second defeated Harsha. Their temples at Aihole, Badami and Pattadakal, a UNESCO site, mark a key stage in temple architecture.
